# AI-TP Project Rules

1. Follow current backend layering: routes -> services -> models/schemas.
2. Keep run/test kind compatibility (`unit/functional/api/perf_*/sec_*/ui`) unless explicitly migrating.
3. Preserve resilient execution semantics: unavailable tools should be `skipped` with reason, not hard-crash the run.
4. Keep status transitions explicit and persisted (`pending/running/completed/failed`).
5. Report generation must include both summary and execution detail (stdout/stderr).
6. Keep backend API-only; avoid reintroducing server-side template rendering.
7. Prefer focused incremental edits; avoid cross-module refactors without clear need.
8. Validate by smoke test after meaningful backend changes.
